      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes numerical drift across batch shapes reported in **#43956**: Qwen3.8-27B scores change enough to flip borderline decisions (FP8 / BF16) when the same token IDs are placed into different batch sizes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe reporter isolated the first projection drift to a pure-PyTorch `torch.nn.functional.linear` (BF16 x BF16 → BF16) in `model.language_model.layers.0.linear_attn.in_proj_ba`. A BF16 intermediate dot product was near the rounding boundary and cuBLAS chose a different reduction order for different M/N/K shapes — this crossed the boundary and the difference propagated through the network. With FP8 checkpoints and the default BF16 LM head the drift reached **12.2 percentage points** on a 0.5 P(positive) tie.\n\n`torch.backends.cuda.matmul.allow_bf16_reduced_precision_reduction = False` alone does not help because the problem is *reduction order*, not reduced-precision reduction.\n\n## Fix\n\nWire cuBLAS and cuDNN determinism into the existing `--enable-deterministic-inference` code path in the argument-resolution pipeline:\n\n1. **`CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG=:4096:8`** — forces cuBLAS to pick the deterministic algorithm variant for every GEMM call, regardless of M/N/K shape. This is the primary fix and is set before any cuBLAS lazy initialisation.\n2. **`CUDNN_DETERMINISTIC=1` / `CUDNN_BENCHMARK=0`** plus the equivalent `torch.backends.cudnn` attributes.\n3. **`torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True, warn_only=True)`** with flash-/mem-efficient-SDP disabled and `allow_bf16_reduced_precision_reduction=False` so remaining PyTorch ops with shape-dependent behaviour are pinned to deterministic code paths.\n\nAll three env vars are applied:\n- First in `handle_deterministic_inference` (pipeline step 228 of 351) — the earliest deterministic hook, well before model load or any GEMM.\n- Then again via `setdefault` in `handle_environment_variables` (step 318) as a belt-and-braces guard for code paths that might initialise cuBLAS between the two steps. `setdefault` preserves the earlier hook’s values.\n\n## Testing\n\nI don’t have access to the reported H20 environment, so verification will need to come from the reporter’s existing reproduction script. The fix is additive to the existing `--enable-deterministic-inference` flag and a no-op when that flag is not set.\n\n## Related\n\nCloses #43956.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38444677950](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38444677950)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38444677764](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38444677764)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38444677940](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38444677940)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
